    "title": "Lansing police identify teenage shooting victim - NewsBreak",
    "text": "By Shajaka Shelton ,\n1 days ago\nLANSING, Mich. (WLNS) — The Lansing Police Department has identified the victim of Tuesday afternoon’s shooting on the south side of the city as Daviahn Lathan, 18.\nAccording to the Lansing Police Department, officers were dispatched to the 2000 block of Georgetown Boulevard at around 2:30 p.m. for a reported shooting.\nThe scene. (WLNS) The scene. (WLNS) The scene. (WLNS) The scene. (WLNS) When officers arrived, they found Lathan with a gunshot wound. Lansing Fire Department responders attempted to provide medical assistance, but he was pronounced dead on scene.\nPolice originally told 6 News a 19-year-old man was arrested in connection with the incident Tuesday afternoon, but Wednesday, they confirmed the suspect is actually a 17-year-old boy.\nPolice are currently attempting to determine what led up to the shooting. The investigation is ongoing.\n6 News will provide updates as they are made available.\nCopyright 2025 Nexstar Media, Inc. All rights reserved. This material may not be published, broadcast, rewritten, or redistributed. For the latest news, weather, sports, and streaming video, head to WLNS 6 News.\n2",
